---
description: Words, plurals, and links in user-facing copy
alwaysApply: true
---

# Copy

Use: folder, question, today, Did I, coins, gems, shop, cheer, streak, Did, Not yet, missed.

Day, not night (owner, 2026-10-14): the screen is "Today", streaks are "days in a row", the previous day is "yesterday". Keep night only where it means nighttime (Night look, Night owl, midnight). Code, keys and routes still say tonight/night.

Never in UI copy: board, hall, hang, heat, skip, nope. The answers are "Did" and "Not yet"; the left button and swipe are "Not yet" (owner, 2026-10-06). A skip reads "Not yet" while its day is open (today, or yesterday until 9am). An answer label stays "Not yet". A day that closed with something open or on Not yet is "Missed" (owner, 2026-10-08). "Nope" is a code name only, never user copy. The waiting state (a question not open yet) is "Later" or "Opens at {time}", never "Not yet". The stored status stays `skip`.

- Plurals: "Did we's", "Did you's" (scripts/check.mjs bans "Did wes"). In plain sentences prefer "shared questions" and "asks from friends".
- Did you questions are typed after a "Did you" label. Anything shown on its own (preview, push, share text) uses `didYouAsk` from `src/lib/link-preview.js`.
- Shared links are full `https://` links (e.g. `https://did-i.app/d/CODE`).
- Short sentences. Concrete nouns. No em dashes.
- No hype: leverage, robust, seamless, unlock, elevate, "60 seconds".
- Every new string goes in all 9 files in `src/locales/` with a real translation, not English.
